WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:02.220
- [Mike] The United States
Air Force Thunderbirds

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:05.220
reached out and asked if I
was ready to fly in an F16.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.477
I reluctantly said yes.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:15.190
I'm gonna pass out.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:16.847
I mean, there's no other way about it.

00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:17.973
I'm gonna pass out.

00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:19.330
- [Lt. Col.] Blood's just
gonna drain out of your skull.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.999
- [Mike] I'm a little dizzy. If we can...

00:00:20.999 --> 00:00:21.832
- [Gator] Okay.

00:00:21.832 --> 00:00:22.665
- [Mike] ...take a quick pause.

00:00:22.665 --> 00:00:23.498
- [Lt. Col.] You feel like you have

00:00:23.498 --> 00:00:24.660
an elephant sitting on your chest.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.910
One, two, three. One, two,
three. One, two, three

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.853
- Had to wake up at 4:00 AM.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.170
So you can bet I didn't sleep much.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.190
Even though the explicit instructions

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.980
were sleep a good night's sleep.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.870
They also said have a heavy breakfast

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.650
or at least a good breakfast.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.760
I had a protein bar. Oh, and a banana.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.540
- We're trying to enter
the air force base.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:54.510
But apparently they said,
we don't know who you are.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.670
Apparently the Pentagon did
not send our clearance through

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.520
to this spot right here.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:03.653
And because of that, oh
my God, plane landing.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.260
I was afraid to do this.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.730
What was I afraid of you may ask.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:08.770
Well, the height for one,

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:10.640
the not knowing what it's
gonna feel like, two,

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:12.670
and three, I was worried about G-LOC.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.680
G-force induce loss of consciousness.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.930
Okay. First of all, what is G-Force?

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:22.040
G-Force is a poorly received
2009 Disney film about a team

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.470
of secret agent Guinea pigs.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:27.230
G-Force is also a measurement
of the force of gravity

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:28.930
on our bodies. In everyday life,

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.000
we have one G of force on us.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.080
That's the earth's
standard force of gravity.

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.090
Our bodies are well acclimated to them.

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:38.000
- So we're going to get
you up to nine Gs today.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.820
A really wicked roller coaster

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:41.720
is like three to four Gs give or take.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.140
At one G, let's say you weigh 200 pounds,

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:46.210
at nine Gs, You can weight 1800 pounds.

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.800
Fluids do what gravity tells them to.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.090
In this case the blood is
gonna drain out of your skull.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.730
- [Mike] So as your heart beats

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:53.490
it's trying to have the blood move up

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.610
but there's way too much
force pushing it down.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.660
As a result, you don't
get enough circulation.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.570
You don't get enough
oxygen going to the brain.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:00.983
You G-LOC, you pass out.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:03.393
- [Instructor] How you feeling, sir?

00:02:03.393 --> 00:02:04.720
The only way to fight that?

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.570
One, I'm going to be
wearing a very special suit

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:10.520
that helps squeeze my lower
body in order to help push some

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.070
of this blood back up into my body.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:13.750
The second thing is something known

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:16.430
as the anti G-straining maneuver.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:19.410
- Ready, now. Good, good,
good clench, good clench.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.870
- Basically what I needed to do

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.290
learn to squeeze my entire lower body

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.330
and try and keep my blood up here.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.610
And you're doing a
breathing technique where

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:32.180
you're exhaling very short
breaths against a closed Glottis.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:37.010
- One, two, three. One two
three. One, two, three.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:38.240
- Because if you don't

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.830
if you let's say go (exhales)

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:41.873
good luck taking a big, deep breath in.

00:02:41.873 --> 00:02:43.367
- You feel like you have an
elephant sitting on your chest.

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:45.680
- This will be the t-shirt
you wear underneath.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.860
This is gonna be your flight suit.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.490
So it's like one big pajama onesie.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:50.323
- Okay.

00:02:50.323 --> 00:02:51.615
- And then these are your boots. Size 11?

00:02:51.615 --> 00:02:52.448
- Yup.

00:02:52.448 --> 00:02:53.281
- All right.

00:02:53.281 --> 00:02:56.070
- They make it sound
so easy. No, it's not.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.930
- [Camera Man] You said
you'll be giggling at nine Gs,

00:02:57.930 --> 00:02:58.763
I think.

00:02:58.763 --> 00:03:00.380
- [Mike] I somehow don't think that's it.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.650
Wait, didn't she say,
"can't have synthetics on"?

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:03.910
I think I'm wearing synthetic underwear.

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:06.120
I haven't worn boots like
this ever in my life.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.310
I would not make a good soldier.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.430
Everyone who wears this patch,

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.440
we have to work our way up to it

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:13.110
So it's an honor to wear this patch

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.506
and today you get to wear it.

00:03:14.506 --> 00:03:15.339
- Wow.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:22.180
I am ready to not eject
out of this aircraft.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:25.763
- Okay, perfect.

00:03:30.637 --> 00:03:32.180
- Do you feel like you have a good seal?

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:33.013
- Yes.

00:03:33.013 --> 00:03:36.563
- Inhale. Hold. One, two, three, exhale.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.060
Yep. And take the helmet off.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.252
Perfect.

00:03:41.252 --> 00:03:42.085
- Cool.

00:03:42.085 --> 00:03:43.170
They taught me about the eject lever

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.500
in between my legs, but
they also consistently

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.010
told me do not pull it unless
you truly need to eject.

00:03:49.010 --> 00:03:51.530
Apparently someone in the
past, they were so anxious

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:54.800
being inside the cockpit, they
just pulled it to escape out.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.940
Next walks in Lieutenant
Colonel, Kevin de Falco.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:01.160
And he tells me everything
we're about to do in this plane.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:04.280
And I'm not gonna lie, my
anxiety was at an all time high.

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.380
I'm gonna pass out.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:07.170
I mean, there's, there's
no other way about it.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:08.003
I'm gonna pass out.

00:04:08.003 --> 00:04:09.690
- You'll be fine. I promise.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.150
If I can do it, you can do it.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.990
I'm like five one, 150 pounds so...

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.050
Yeah. but that makes it better for you.

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:18.345
You're more protected from the G-Force.

00:04:18.345 --> 00:04:20.530
- That's true, that's
true. Short and female.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.540
- To be honest, like they sound

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.440
very reassuring when they talk to you.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:28.770
But I think that the
reassurance, maybe one of those,

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:31.840
like make him think he'll
be okay so he will be okay.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.590
So I don't think I'm gonna be okay.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.269
But I might be okay.

00:04:37.269 --> 00:04:39.852
(upbeat music)

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.800
- [Camera Man] Famous last words?

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.722
- This was a bad idea.

00:05:15.722 --> 00:05:18.639
(drumline playing)

00:05:27.405 --> 00:05:30.072
(radio chatter)

00:05:32.514 --> 00:05:35.014
- [Gator] There's afterburner.

00:05:36.305 --> 00:05:38.555
There's 100 miles per hour.

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:41.701
There's 150.

00:05:42.766 --> 00:05:44.827
We're gonna take off here.

00:05:44.827 --> 00:05:46.160
Gears coming up.

00:05:49.328 --> 00:05:51.050
There's 250 miles an hour.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.858
Take a breath.

00:05:52.858 --> 00:05:56.419
Here come the Gs.

00:05:56.419 --> 00:05:59.086
(radio chatter)

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:11.132
All right, so yeah, if you look at the...

00:06:11.132 --> 00:06:12.958
We're going about .67 machs,

00:06:12.958 --> 00:06:14.860
about 67% the speed of sound.

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:16.029
- [Mike] That's in the bottom left corner.

00:06:16.029 --> 00:06:17.837
- [Gator] Bottom left corner, yeah.

00:06:17.837 --> 00:06:19.450
303 knots. I can switch
that to ground speed.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:23.208
We're going 395 miles
per hour ground speed.

00:06:23.208 --> 00:06:24.890
1G currently.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:25.770
Ready to go?

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:26.603
- [Mike] Yup.

00:06:26.603 --> 00:06:27.436
- All right, good prep.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:29.770
Here come the Gs.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.570
- I'm starting to lose my vision.

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:40.520
My heart is working in overdrive
to try and bring the blood

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.794
back from my lower body to my brain.

00:06:42.794 --> 00:06:44.250
- [Gator] All right, next
we're going into a loop.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.290
You ready to go for the loop?

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:46.123
- [Mike] Okay.

00:06:46.123 --> 00:06:46.956
- [Gator] Deep breath.

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:48.990
Here come the Gs.

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:58.370
- Staring inside the cockpit
was a really bad idea.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.330
It causes sensory conflict
between what my eyes were seeing

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:03.620
and what my inner equilibrium was feeling.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.780
As a result, I got really nauseous.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:08.143
- [Gator] Gonna bring
it all the way through.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.490
We're gonna keep going.
You can see our smoke.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:14.693
There's our smoke. Look up
and you can see the smoke.

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:18.233
There's our loop, how
about that? Pretty cool!

00:07:18.233 --> 00:07:20.415
- [Mike] I'm a little dizzy. If we can...

00:07:20.415 --> 00:07:21.248
- [Gator] Okay.

00:07:21.248 --> 00:07:22.081
- [Mike] ...take a quick pause.

00:07:22.081 --> 00:07:22.914
- [Gator] All right.

00:07:22.914 --> 00:07:23.747
- [Mike] Recalibrate here.

00:07:23.747 --> 00:07:25.320
- [Gator] Yeah. All right,
we're gonna get down here

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:26.850
and we're gonna do a knife edge next.

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:27.683
- [Mike] Okay.

00:07:27.683 --> 00:07:28.516
- [Gator] Ready to go?

00:07:28.516 --> 00:07:29.377
- [Mike] Yup.

00:07:29.377 --> 00:07:32.044
- [Gator] All right, here we go.

00:07:32.894 --> 00:07:35.870
Through the clouds at a 90 degree angle.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:37.059
Nice and straight.

00:07:37.059 --> 00:07:39.204
We're gonna streak down
now, left side, ready?

00:07:39.204 --> 00:07:40.159
- [Mike] Yup.

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:43.348
- [Gator] Here we go,
inverted to inverted.

00:07:43.348 --> 00:07:46.003
Inverted. We'll hang here.

00:07:46.003 --> 00:07:48.096
All right, you ready to roll 360 degrees?

00:07:48.096 --> 00:07:48.929
- [Mike] Yeah.

00:07:48.929 --> 00:07:51.700
- [Gator] Here we go. Rolling it.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:53.253
Here we go, inverted again.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.130
Take a look at the
clouds, we're past them.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:56.963
- [Mike] Yeah.

00:07:56.963 --> 00:07:58.460
- [Gator] Good breath.

00:07:58.460 --> 00:07:59.483
Here come the Gs.

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:09.486
(suspenseful music)

00:08:28.063 --> 00:08:31.010
(cheering and applause)

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:32.450
- He was a little nervous this morning

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.120
about what the maneuvers are gonna be like

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:35.820
and how we were gonna do,

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:36.740
but I'll tell you, he got through

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:39.365
the entire profile today.
We did every maneuver.

00:08:39.365 --> 00:08:40.600
(cheering and applause)

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:42.055
You guys are probably
curious on what he did

00:08:42.055 --> 00:08:45.770
in terms of Gs. He did pull 9.2 Gs.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:49.103
(cheering and applause)

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:53.120
- It could not have been
done without everyone here.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.930
So I have to give everyone a
huge thank you for allowing me

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:59.110
to participate, this is a
once in a lifetime experience

00:08:59.110 --> 00:09:02.000
that I'm gonna be telling
my followers, my patients.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:02.833
So thank you again.

00:09:02.833 --> 00:09:04.998
And thank you, Gator, for
getting me back safely.

00:09:04.998 --> 00:09:05.831
- Yeah.

00:09:05.831 --> 00:09:08.183
Thanks for keeping
everybody healthy and happy

00:09:08.183 --> 00:09:11.460
and inspiring your followers
to live a better life.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.360
That's important to us too.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.600
- [Mike] I was so nervous.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.950
- I know, I was a little worried.

00:09:15.950 --> 00:09:18.150
You were so nervous during the briefings.

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:21.920
- Right. After that first
one I knew I could handle it.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:25.440
Came close to graying out a
couple of times, but I noticed

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:28.770
as I adjusted my muscles
and I wasn't squeezing,

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:31.270
I would say, my abdomen
enough, or my glutes enough.

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:34.390
Once I adjusted, right
away, the vision came back.

00:09:34.390 --> 00:09:36.680
Let's get this video to
a 100 thousand likes.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:40.650
Let's continue our mission with
the United States air force.

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:41.840
Let's see some cool stuff.

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:43.430
Let's see the medical side of it.

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:46.670
Let's see what being a doctor
in the air force is like

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:49.570
- I'm working and flying
everyday with my patients.

00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:51.560
- You wanna do that, definitely hit like.

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.450
Check out this video of me
saving a life on an airplane,

00:09:54.450 --> 00:09:57.930
or this video here where I
actually fly a different airplane

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.380
and hold some incredible animals.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:01.680
Actually interact with the animal.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.490
Like, both are really good watches.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:04.490
Which one are you going to watch?

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:06.313
As always stay happy and healthy.

